<!--
    Copyright 2026 Revenax Digital Services
    Author: Mohamed A. Abdallah
    Website: https://www.revenax.com

    Keep "Reload Data" in the POS burger menu at ALL times.

    Stock Odoo renders that item with t-if="!this.pos.data.network.offline", so
    it vanishes the moment the register believes it is offline. It is NOT
    access-gated (its siblings Install App / Cash In/Out check
    cashier._role != 'minimal'; this one never did), so the disappearance staff
    reported was the offline flag, not permissions.

    That guard is backwards for this shop: a register that has gone stale or
    wrongly thinks it is offline is exactly when the cashier needs to force a
    reload. Hiding the control leaves them stuck with no recourse but closing
    the session. Reloading while genuinely offline just surfaces a normal
    network error, which is a far better outcome than a missing button.

    Overriding the attribute (rather than adding a second item) keeps ONE entry
    in the menu — no duplicate when online.
-->
<templates id="template" xml:space="preserve">

    <t t-inherit="point_of_sale.Navbar" t-inherit-mode="extension">
        <xpath expr="//DropdownItem[contains(text(), 'Reload Data')]" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="t-if">true</attribute>
        </xpath>
    </t>

</templates>
